WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.051
Local execution does not automatically create security.

00:00:04.051 --> 00:00:16.202
A server bound to all network interfaces, an unauthenticated web UI, weak remote access, or shared administrator credentials can expose prompts, documents, and compute.

00:00:16.202 --> 00:00:25.971
Use individual accounts, least privilege, strong authentication, segmentation, encrypted connections where appropriate, secure administration, request limits, and audit logs.

00:00:25.971 --> 00:00:30.022
Keep the inference API off untrusted networks.

00:00:30.022 --> 00:00:38.361
Protect API keys, service credentials, database passwords, encryption keys, and integration tokens in approved secret storage.

00:00:38.361 --> 00:00:41.459
Give each tool narrow permissions.

00:00:41.459 --> 00:00:47.415
Agent tools can turn a model mistake into an external action.

00:00:47.415 --> 00:00:55.278
Prompts, uploads, outputs, retrieved passages, embeddings, histories, caches, telemetry, and logs may contain sensitive data.

00:00:55.278 --> 00:01:01.712
Define collection, access, retention, backup, export, redaction, and deletion for each category.

00:01:01.712 --> 00:01:07.668
Treat model, embedding, interface, plugin, and runtime downloads as supply-chain inputs.

00:01:07.668 --> 00:01:17.437
Use trusted sources, review licenses and provenance, validate expected files where appropriate, patch dependencies, and avoid unknown execution scripts.

00:01:17.437 --> 00:01:24.347
Protect the knowledge base and backups to the same standard as source documents.

00:01:24.347 --> 00:01:27.445
Test restoration and access revocation.

00:01:27.445 --> 00:01:34.831
Private means the full data lifecycle is controlled, including failure, support, export, and retirement.

00:01:34.831 --> 00:01:38.881
Plugins and tools expand the trust boundary.

00:01:38.881 --> 00:01:44.362
Review their code, permissions, destinations, update path, and error behavior.

00:01:44.362 --> 00:01:52.224
Require confirmation for consequential actions and prevent a model from silently broadening its own access.
